       <div class="ch">
    
    <h1>Astable Multivibrator (Relaxation Oscillator) - SPICE Time Domain Analysis</h1>

    <div class="ch-card">
        <h2>Circuit Components</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Op-Amp:</strong> TL084 (operational amplifier)</li>
            <li><strong>R1:</strong> 1 kΩ (feedback resistor to inverting input)</li>
            <li><strong>R2:</strong> 1 kΩ (positive feedback resistor)</li>
            <li><strong>R3:</strong> 1 kΩ (reference resistor to ground)</li>
            <li><strong>C1:</strong> 1 μF (timing capacitor)</li>
            <li><strong>V1:</strong> +10V (positive supply)</li>
            <li><strong>V2:</strong> -10V (negative supply)</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <h2>Oscillation Frequency Calculation</h2>
    <div class="ch-formula">
        β = R3 / (R2 + R3) = 1k / (1k + 1k) = 0.5<br>
        Threshold voltages: Vth+ = +5V, Vth- = -5V<br>
        T = 2RC × ln((1+β)/(1-β)) = 2 × 1k × 1μF × ln(3) ≈ <strong>2.2 ms</strong><br>
        f = 1/T ≈ <strong>455 Hz</strong>
    </div>
    
    <div id="circuit"></div>
    <div id="plot1"></div>

    <h2>Simulation Results</h2>
    <div class="ch-grid">

        <div class="ch-col blue">
            <h3>Capacitor Voltage V(in) - Blue</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Exponential charging/discharging waveform</li>
                <li>Oscillates between approximately -4V and +4V</li>
                <li>Charges toward +10V when output is HIGH</li>
                <li>Discharges toward -10V when output is LOW</li>
                <li>Switches direction at ±5V thresholds</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="ch-col red">
            <h3>Output Voltage V(out) - Red</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Square wave oscillating between +10V and -10V</li>
                <li>Period ≈ 2.2 ms (frequency ≈ 455 Hz)</li>
                <li>50% duty cycle (symmetric oscillation)</li>
                <li>Switches when capacitor voltage reaches thresholds</li>
                <li>Rail-to-rail output swing</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

    </div>

    <div class="ch-card green-border">
        <h2>Conclusion</h2>
        <p style="line-height: 1.6; margin: 0;">This circuit is an <strong>Astable Multivibrator</strong> (Relaxation Oscillator) using a TL084 op-amp. The circuit generates continuous oscillation without any external input signal. The capacitor C1 charges and discharges through R1, while the positive feedback network (R2, R3) creates two threshold voltages at ±5V. When the capacitor voltage reaches +5V, the output switches from +10V to -10V, causing the capacitor to discharge. When it reaches -5V, the output switches back to +10V, and the cycle repeats. This creates a self-sustaining oscillation at approximately 455 Hz, producing both a square wave output and a triangular/exponential waveform at the capacitor.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="ch-card" style="background-color: #e8f8f5; border-left: 4px solid #1abc9c;">
        <h2 style="color: #16a085;">Operating Principle</h2>
        <ul style="line-height: 1.6; margin: 0;">
            <li><strong>Positive Feedback:</strong> Creates hysteresis with two switching thresholds</li>
            <li><strong>RC Timing:</strong> Capacitor charging/discharging determines oscillation period</li>
            <li><strong>No Stable State:</strong> Circuit continuously switches between two states</li>
            <li><strong>Frequency Control:</strong> Adjust R1 or C1 to change oscillation frequency</li>
            <li><strong>Applications:</strong> Clock generation, tone generation, timing circuits, LED flashers</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

